INT. NEXUS ARENA - FINALS STAGE - NIGHT

A packed esports arena. Strobing blue light. Two gaming rigs on a raised platform, a huge screen above.

WREN, 20s, hoodie, headset around her neck, sits dead still. Her coach HALE, 50s, crouches beside her chair.

ADMIN (V.O.)
(over the PA)
Match four, final round. Players, please confirm your connection.

In the crowd, a TEENAGE BOY lowers his phone. An old SECURITY GUARD scans the aisles, bored.

ANGLE ON THE SCREEN

Wren's character, a knight, stands in an empty grey corridor. There is no opponent's name in the lobby.

ON SCREEN: PLAYER 2 HAS JOINED (0 ms)

HALE
(quiet)
Wren. Look at me.

WREN
I'm looking at it.

HALE
No. At me.

She does. (beat)

HALE (CONT'D)
Twelve years I've done this. I have seen every kind of cheat there is. Lag switches, ghost accounts, a kid who taped a second keyboard under his desk. And I've been telling you since the qualifiers that something is wrong, and you keep saying "it's just a bug." You're a better player than a bug.

WREN
It is a bug.

HALE
(beat)
Then why did it say your mother's name in the chat?

CLOSE ON the chat window. A single line.

ON SCREEN: > hello wren. you left the door open.

Wren pulls her hands off the keyboard. Hale grabs the cable. The screen doesn't flicker. The game keeps playing without them.

THE CROWD
(chanting, rising)
WREN! WREN! WREN!

The teenage boy drops his drink. The guard turns, hand to his radio.

WE SEE every monitor in the arena flip to the same grey corridor. The knight turns, slowly, to the camera.

ADMIN (V.O.)
(over the PA, strange, soft)
Please remain seated. We are experiencing a technical difficulty.

HALE
Get up. Wren. Get up.

WREN
(very calm)
If I stand up it gets in here.

BACK TO SCENE

Hale stares at her. The strobes slow. Stop.

THE CROWD
(a whisper, all at once)
Wren.

The doors of the arena clank shut. Every single one. Wren pulls the headset onto her ears.

WREN (CONT'D)
(beat)
Tell my mother I'm sorry about the name.

She picks up the controller. The knight raises its sword.

HALE
Don't.

Everyone in the front row stands and sits down in unison.

FADE OUT.
